      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> to prevent creating a possible fraud vector\n\nI'm sure I don't have to recite the age-old \"security through obscurity is no security at all\" adage.\n\nThis is the primary reason that digital age verification systems are so problematic. Everyone's so thirsty for the data mining that nobody's bothered to engineer a trustworthy verification scaffold.\n\nFor dog's sake, VRChat, there has to be a better way than this.",
