      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Another update on my situation:\n\nI have finally figured out what is going on with my verification. In my country there are certain laws when it comes to organisations requesting identity documents online. Thus I have been submitting my identity documents in the manner that our regulatory authority recommends.\n\nHowever, the system VRChat uses appears to require an identity document that is unaltered or at least displays information they are not allowed to process. I have contacted Persona legal about this. They directed me to VRChat legal who have yet to respond to my inquiry.\n\nI know this because it appears that identity documents are stored in a format that can be viewed by employees of Persona for some unknown amount of time if verification doesn’t succeed.\n\nI am disappointed that VRChat has displayed so little urgency in addressing this issue and shocked that personal information is being stored (however briefly) in a manner that is so open to abuse.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-04-28T08:29:38.548Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The automated system Persona uses fails to identify any form of ID I provide. Despite using every form of ID that’s available to me and trying it under different lighting conditions I get the same result.\n\nThis system seems to have no way of falling back on some other form of age verification. The extent of customer support I’ve gotten on this subject so far is being told to try again.\n\nAre there plans to provide alternative methods of age verification so that people don’t get unfairly excluded through no fault of their own?",
